<title>USA: Heilig-Meyers buys mattress retailer.</title>
<headline>Heilig-Meyers buys mattress retailer.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Heilig-Meyers Co., a furniture retailer, said Tuesday it has signed a letter of intent to buy Mattress Discounters, a 165-outlet retailer of bedding, for an undisclosed amount.</p>
<p>Heilig-Meyers said that Mattress Discounters, based in Upper Marlboro, Md., has annual sales of $175 million.</p>
<p>Financial details will be announced when a definitive acquisition agreement reached, the company said.</p>
<p>Heilig-Meyers' stock was unchanged at $18.875 on the New York Stock Exchange.</p>
</text>
